Explanation:

- We detect the special case of replacing an already‐collapsed subprocess.
- If the old subprocess was collapsed (`!isExpanded(oldBusinessObject)`), we explicitly copy over its current `element.width`/`height` into the new element.
- This prevents the replacement from snapping back to the default size of the target type (e.g. Ad Hoc SubProcess).
